/*
 * Little Hafiz Quest: content data
 * ================================
 * Everything the game teaches lives in this one file. It is plain data: no code runs here.
 *
 * window.LHQ_DATA = {
 *   version:   data format version.
 *   bismillah: the Arabic text of the Basmalah (Sūrah 1, āyah 1).
 *   surahs: [   in learning order, from 114 (An-Nās) up to 78 (An-Naba’).
 *     {
 *       n:       sūrah number. (The Hidden Garden's stops, after An-Naba’, use keys 201–206 instead: their own
 *                garden: true, sura: the real sūrah number, from: the first āyah's number when it isn't 1, and
 *                bism: false where no Basmalah comes before them.)
 *       ar:      Arabic name.
 *       name:    transliterated name.        meaning: English meaning of the name.
 *       icon:    one emoji for the map island. theme:  a kid-friendly place name for the island.
 *       color:   island color (#rrggbb).
 *       pattern: a short memory trick for the grown-up (may contain <b> tags).
 *       toy:     (optional) [emoji, sound] a button the child taps along with the trick, e.g. ["🔔", "bell"].
 *                Sounds: bell, clap, drum, chime, pop, boop, whoosh, hum (see sfx in js/game.js).
 *       parts:   checkpoints as [firstĀyah, lastĀyah] pairs (1-based, covering every āyah once, in order).
 *       ayat: [  one object per āyah, in order:
 *         ar:      Uthmani Arabic text (do not edit by hand).
 *         tr:      simple transliteration.
 *         kid:     a one-sentence meaning a 5-year-old can follow.
 *         scene:   1–3 emoji: the picture cue.   hook: a 1–4 word name for the picture.
 *         gesture: emoji + a hand action to do while reciting.
 *         anim:    how the picture moves (see the .an-* classes in css/game.css).
 *         twin:    (optional) number of the āyah with exactly the same words.
 *       ]
 *     }
 *   ],
 * }
 * Recitation timings are not here: each reciter has audio/<reciter>/timings.json (see tools/build_audio.py).
 *
 * Editing tips
 *   - Change a picture, action or meaning by editing that āyah's line below.
 *   - Within a sūrah, every scene should be different (except "twin" āyāt), so the puzzles stay fair.
 *   - After any change, bump VERSION in sw.js so installed copies pick it up.
 *
 * Sources and licenses (see README.md)
 *   - Arabic text: quran-json by Risan Bagja Pradana (Uthmani text from The Noble Qur'an Encyclopedia,
 *     quranenc.com), CC BY-SA 4.0. This file is an adaptation and is shared under CC BY-SA 4.0 too.
 *     Open tanwīn marks were converted to the standard Unicode characters (U+08F0–U+08F2).
 *     The Hidden Garden's text (v2.12.0): Quran.com's KFGQPC Hafs text (text_qpc_hafs), converted to the same
 *     convention (checked to give exactly the text above for all 564 āyāt of Juz ʿAmma).
 *   - Memory cues, simple meanings and transliterations: written for this project.
 */
